      "name": "retry-backoff",
      "title": "consulted: reference material nobody performs — a PRINCIPLE, not a procedure: every heading is an argument (\"Retrying a definitive answer is not caution\", \"Jitter is not decoration here\"), and it names no actor and no trigger. It is read when writing retry code, never performed as a step.",
      "description": "Every error gets a falling-off retry rate — each wait doubles, with jitter. Read before writing any call that can fail transiently, and before deciding that a failure is worth retrying at all. Exhausting the retries does not change the verdict.",
